+            //
+            // THE HEIGHT THE PROMISE IS ABOUT IS THE ONE THE RENDERER LAYS OUT, not the
+            // w:trHeight this row declares. hRule is "atLeast", so a row whose cells hold more
+            // line boxes than the declared height accounts for is GROWN by the renderer, and a
+            // rule keyed on the declared height calls such a row safe when it is not. That is
+            // exactly 041122's breaking row: declared 2220 tw (111 pt) at a top edge of 683.6,
